cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the preferred q18/g37 historical article for its quantitative security claims, and cite the separate V5 release reference for the later source-linked Tag-67 mainnet result."
title: "Aspis: From Lean-Checked Private-Spend Mathematics to Solana Mainnet"
type: software
date-released: 2026-07-25
authors:
  - family-names: "Barker"
    given-names: "Dominic"
    website: "https://github.com/DJBarker87"
abstract: >-
  Aspis connects maintained Lean 4 private-spend mathematics to selected
  production verifier paths translated through Charon/Aeneas and joined to
  the models by explicit bridge proofs, then to a byte-reproducible
  1,258,496-byte Solana SBF binary. The
  finalized V5 Tag-67 mainnet transaction verified a 75,358-byte proof and
  consumed 1,334,452 compute units in both exact simulation and landed
  metadata. The distinct q18/g37 historical release carries the manuscript's
  100.161-bit work-normalized soundness floor, 104.024-bit
  real-versus-simulator floor, and 103.024-bit pairwise-witness floor. The
  source correspondence covers a selected release schedule and retains one
  explicit transcript-hash-call equality; compiler, extraction toolchain,
  Solana runtime, SHA-256, random-oracle, and cited primitive assumptions
  remain. The project has not received an external security audit.
keywords:
